==Latin==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|la|dem}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*domos}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*dṓm|t=house, home}}, from root {{m|ine-pro|*dem-|t=to build}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|δόμος}}, {{cog|sq|dhomë|t=a chamber, a room}}, {{cog|ae|𐬨𐬀𐬛|tr=dam-}} {{cog|sa|दम|tr=dáma}} and {{cog|sla-pro|*domъ}}. The same [[Proto-Indo-European]] root also gave {{cog|ang|timber|t=building, act of building}}; see modern {{cog|en|timber}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=1}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|domus|domūs|gen2=domī|f|fourth|decl2=second}}

# [[house]], [[home]]
#: {{syn|la|aedēs|casa|domicilium|habitātiō|mānsiō|sēdēs|tēctum}}
#: {{hyper|la|aedificium|cōnstructiō}}
#: {{hypo|la|domuncula|tugurium}}
#* Motto of [[w:Methodist Ladies' College, Melbourne|Methodist Ladies' College, Melbourne]]
#*: ''Deo '''domui'''[[-que|que]].''
#*:: For God and for '''home'''.
#* First part of the motto of [[w:Harrow School|Harrow School]], [[w:England|England]]
#*: ''Stet fortuna '''domus'''.''
#*:: Let the fortune of the '''house''' stand.
# {{lb|la|poetic}} any [[building]] or [[abode]]
#: {{syn|la|aedificium|cōnstructiō}}
# [[native]] place, one's [[country]] or [[home]] (confer [[patria]])
# [[household]], [[family]], [[race]]

====Usage notes====
* '''Domus''' is one of a handful of common nouns that take the [[locative case]], others are [[rus#Latin|rus]] and [[humus#Latin|humus]]. It is irregular in that it has a mix of second and fourth declension forms, the second declension forms being more commonly used in place constructions.

====Declension====
{{la-decl-irreg|noun=1|domus}}

* At least in later Latin, the most common declension is as follows:
: ''domus, domus, domui, domum, domo — domus, domorum, domibus, domos, domibus''.

